  "markdown_content": "Indian startup Inshorts, which began as a news aggregation platform, has successfully raised $60 million in a new financing round. The funding comes as a validation of the company's strategic expansion into social media with its app called Public, launched two years ago.\\n\\nThe startup confirmed the investment, which signals growing investor confidence in Inshorts' ability to diversify beyond its core news aggregation service. The Public app, their social networking venture, has shown promising growth metrics since its launch, contributing to investor interest in the company.\\n\\nInshorts has managed to establish itself in the Indian digital media landscape, first through its concise news delivery format, and now through its social networking initiative. The fresh capital is expected to fuel further expansion and development of both platforms.\\n\\n## Key Highlights\\n* Raised $60 million in new financing round\\n* Successfully expanded into social media with \"Public\" app\\n* Strong growth metrics reported for social networking venture\\n* Capital to be used for platform expansion and development",
